os-dev-report
{
 "issue": 15214,
 "status": "done",
 "branch": "claude/issue-15214-c11-fresh-install-docs",
 "pr": "https://github.com/objectstack-ai/objectstack/pull/24506 (docs + riders, head 77a7a78ab); https://github.com/objectstack-ai/objectstack/pull/24507 (ADR-0131 D14 dated note only, branch claude/issue-15214-c11-d14-note, head c6c8dd65f, Tier H: the maintainer merges)",
 "session": "session_01L9ZWcgyzEyyKR2nnDzto54 (dispatched by the epic seat session_01Y5583bs2RDd53MH6kM1ca3; the newest Claim on #15214 is 6261901354 and names this branch, verified before work)",
 "premise_still_valid": true,
 "summary": "PR 24506 has the docs and the riders. The tenancy page gains 'Who owns a row': ADR-0131's three rules, 18.0 single stamping under 8b's ruling (stamped with the Default Organization, or refused for zero or several organizations), and a callout answering the platform-tables question of 11611. The existing 18.0 callout gains two facts: 18.0 databases take the 18.x path, and the walled refusal covers the os boot path only (one-shot boots and embedded hosts are not refused and are not supported walled deployments). The posture table's single cell 'filled in on write: no' is corrected. NULL-as-global wording is reworded in sharing-rules, permissions-matrix, rls and system-context row 23d, and in the SQL driver's applyTenantScope docblock (comment only). The riders: one sentence in organizationOwnershipRefusalMessage; TENANCY_POSTURE_FIX_HINTS keeps group and isolated but suffixes '; refused at boot in 18.0, which supports single only'; os doctor adds a 'Tenancy posture' warning row under a walled posture. The changeset is .changeset/15214-c11-fresh-install-messages.md, patch for cli and runtime. PR 24507 adds the D14 dated note (sprint 6259899486, 18.0 databases on the 18.x path, the walled refusal on the os boot path only, C11 off the gate per 6261853191), with maintainer quotes verbatim. No file of 8b's branch (36 files, fetched at af977a6), of open PR 24482, of serve.ts or of migrate/organization-ownership.ts is touched, so no rider was dropped. No card close-out, comment or label write was made on 13564, 13636, PR 14923, 11611 or 10103.",
 "tests": "At 77a7a78ab, whose tree is byte-identical to the measured tree. Lock: pnpm --filter '@objectstack/cli^...' build gave VERDICT command-exit 0. cli unit (vitest --project unit): 308/312 files passed in the first run. The 4 others are outside the diff: boot-preparation-parity and hook-timeout-override-refusal hit 'Test timed out in 5000ms' under gate-sweep load; published-subpath-console and published-subpath-hook-body said 'packages/cli is not built'. After pnpm --filter @objectstack/cli build they were rerun: the 2 published-subpath files passed, and the 2 timeout files passed (2/2 files, 41/41 tests, VERDICT 0). cli typecheck: exit 0. runtime test: 421/421 files, 6643 passed, 19 skipped. runtime typecheck: exit 0. Pins moved: serve site 6 and doctor leg (i) and the CONTROL carry the 18.0 suffix. The doctor-tenancy-posture-report and doctor-env-provenance controls moved from isolated to single, because 'a posture that can start' is false for isolated in 18.0. New: a walledPostureFinding sweep and an in-process os doctor run under group (warning, exit 0). The boot-guard test asserts the 18.0/17.x answer appears ahead of the command. No ablation: only message strings and a new advisory row changed. cli integration tier: declared to CI (no integration-tier or spawn-entry file touched).",
 "gates": "PR 24506: dispatch-gates --commands named 102 families, plus 48 roster commands on stderr. All 150 were run, exit codes captured before any pipe. --ran: '102 derived famil(ies) accounted for — 102 run, 0 NOT-MEASURED (a DERIVED zero — all 102 recorded an exit code and none of them is 3)'. Seven first answered exit 3 (PREREQUISITE NOT MET: missing dist, or a shallow fixture). After building client-react, studio and 6 packages, and fetching 621a4876, all seven exit 0. Four roster gates need PR or workflow context: closing-target-claim, partof-closing-keyword, single-claim-paths, governed-queue-guard (exit 2/1, NOT WIRED). partof-closing-keyword with this PR body as PR_BODY exits 0. PR 24507: 19 derived plus 55 roster, all run; --ran 19/19, 0 NOT-MEASURED. check:doc-formula-expressions is 0 after building lint. check:dts-closure and check:published-readme-exports are NOT MEASURED there (prerequisite, no builds in that worktree). partof-closing-keyword with the body: exit 0. CI at report time: 24506 head 77a7a78ab has 38 check-runs: 5 success, 5 skipped, 27 in_progress, 1 queued, 0 failed. 24507 head c6c8dd65f has 22: 1 success, 1 skipped, 20 in_progress, 0 failed. Conclusions are in_progress; the seat reads CI convergence. NOT MEASURED locally, CI's: Build Docs, Build Core, the Test Core shards, the type-check lanes.",
 "mcp_calls": "0 — every GitHub read was an unauthenticated REST GET to api.github.com; no MCP tool was called",
 "api_writes": "3 relay strokes (POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches). Stroke 1 (run 39227453121): POST /pulls x2 (24506, 24507) and POST /issues/{n}/assignees x2 (os-steve), both read back byte-identical. Stroke 2 (run 39227687975): this report, POST /issues/15214/comments x1 (comment 6263677182). Stroke 3: PATCH /issues/comments/6263677182, correcting this field, which first said 3 strokes when 2 had been sent. git push is not counted: 2 branches, plus one --force-with-lease on the docs branch to squash its own WIP commits before any PR existed (all five §3 criteria held; the tree was byte-identical)",
 "open_questions": [
  {
   "question": "os doctor: warning or error for a walled posture in 18.0?",
   "options": [
    "A warning (taken): exit code unchanged, the row names the os serve refusal; one-shot commands doctor fronts still boot walled",
    "B error: mirrors the unrecognized-posture finding's rule that doctor must not call an environment serve refuses 'functional'; changes doctor's exit code for walled environments"
   ],
   "recommendation": "A, taken. The row is temporary (the 18.x restore deletes it, with the serve refusal). serve's refusal is already loud and fatal. An exit-code change is a bigger operator-facing face than this rider's 'add the 18.0 sentence'. B is a one-word change if the seat prefers it."
  },
  {
   "question": "Card sentence 2 says 'the column is NOT NULL'. 8e (NOT NULL) moved to 18.x per 6259698357 item 3. How should the docs word it?",
   "options": [
    "A (taken): 'every such row carries its organization; NULL is not an owner', without claiming the DDL constraint",
    "B: state NOT NULL now, which is false for an 18.0 database"
   ],
   "recommendation": "A, taken. The 18.x docs pass can add the constraint wording when 8e lands."
  },
  {
   "question": "TENANCY_POSTURE_FIX_HINTS: drop group and isolated from the fix list, or say they are refused?",
   "options": [
    "A (taken): keep them, with the suffix '; refused at boot in 18.0, which supports single only' (one constant, WALLED_POSTURE_RELEASE_NOTE, that the 18.x restore deletes)",
    "B: drop them from the list in 18.0"
   ],
   "recommendation": "A, taken. It is the smaller truthful change: the list enumerates the posture vocabulary, and two pins assert every posture is listed."
  },
  {
   "question": "A dispatch-word conflict about the boot-guard pins",
   "options": [
    "The dispatch said 'update its test pins'; os-dev.md says message prose is not pinned beyond named subjects"
   ],
   "recommendation": "os-dev.md followed. The new assertion checks the named subjects (the '18.0 does not upgrade a v17 database' clause and '17.x release until the 18.x release') and their order ahead of the command, not the full prose."
  }
 ],
 "out_of_scope_findings": [
  "class: none (noted, not filed) · docs outside the tenancy and permissions pages still describe the COALESCE(organization_id, '__global__') index key and the NULL partition (data-modeling/indexing.mdx, protocol/objectql/schema.mdx, deployment/seed-tenancy-repair.mdx, deployment/cli.mdx). The mechanism is live in 18.0 (8d moved to 18.x), so the pages are true today · carrier: none · noted in PR 24506 Acceptance notes",
  "class: none (noted, not filed) · system-context.mdx row 62 (the organizations plugin's elevated insert landing NULL under a wall) is walled-posture text, left as is because 18.0 refuses walled boots · carrier: none · noted in PR 24506 Acceptance notes",
  "deviation: an unquoted shell heredoc in this session expanded backtick spans while editing the PR 2 body draft. It ran one read-only dispatch-gates derivation in the primary checkout, which found nothing to derive; the other fragments failed as command-not-found. Nothing was written to the repository, and the body was rewritten before the PR was created"
 ]
}
